CloudBurrow patch 12 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1230).

The bug: a query that failed as it ran, such as SELECT ERROR('boom'),
failed "failed to scan rows: boom": Repository.Query wrapped the error
its rows gave (rows.Err) in its own words. BigQuery fails such a query
with the error alone, "boom", in jobs.query's error, in a query job's
status.errorResult and errors, and in a script's @@error.message
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/debugging_functions#error).

The patch returns the rows' error as it is.

